/* book: lead: The convolution integral gives the output of a continuous-time LTI system from its input x(t) and its impulse response h(t): y(t)=x(t)*h(t). It adds up one shifted, scaled copy of h for every instant of the input. To evaluate it, flip h, slide it across x, multiply the two where they overlap and take the area. Engineers use it to predict a filter's response to a pulse, a loudspeaker's response to  */
