/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Here x*h means ∫−∞∞x(τ)h(t−τ)dτ, with τ the dummy variable and t the output time.
   - The analogy with multiplication stops at division.
   - Shift: if x(t)*h(t)=y(t), then x(t−t₁)*h(t−t₂)=y(t−t₁−t₂).
   - Width: if x is nonzero only on ax≤t≤bx and h only on ah≤t≤bh, then y is nonzero only on ax+ah≤t≤bx+bh.
   - Two rectangles: heights Ax and Ah, widths Tx and Th, give a trapezoid of peak AxAh·min(Tx, Th); equal widths give a triangle.
   - Derivative and integral: d/dt(x*h)=(dx/dt)*h=x*(dh/dt), and the running integral of x*h equals (running integral of x)*h.
*/
