/* book exam traps: Causal does not imply stable: u(t) is zero for t<0 but its area is infinite. | Stable does not imply causal: e2tu(−t) has finite area 1/2 but is nonzero before t=0. | Leaving out the absolute value: the ideal low-pass impulse response h(t)=sin(t)/(πt) has net area exactly 1, yet the area under |h(t)| is infinite, so it is not BIBO stable. | Causality allows h(0)≠0; it forbids only t<0. δ(t) itself is causal. | BIBO is tested on h(t), not on one chosen input. A single bounded input that gives a bounded output proves nothing. */
